</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Caspary</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Down-regulation of inhibition following unilateral deafening</article-title><source>Hear Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>147</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>187</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10962184</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-5955(00)00054-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vale</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Juiz</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanes</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Unilateral cochlear ablation produces greater loss of inhibition in the contralateral inferior colliculus</article-title><source>Eur J Neurosci</source><year>2004</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>2133</fpage><lpage>2140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15450092</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1460-9568.2004.03679.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Illing</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraus</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Meidinger</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reconnecting neuronal networks in the auditory brainstem following unilateral deafening</article-title><source>Hear Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>206</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>199</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16081008</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.heares.2005.01.016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anders